From 0cd980f852f7724fe59e7afb837730da5677d0e1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 00:26:49 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09275/11362] Turn scored MTP off, because Qwen3.8-27B has no
 draft head

Kernel v19 ran the new configuration on the scored card and reported the
disagreement itself:

  LLM TIER MTP DECLARED-VS-ACTUAL MISMATCH: SUBMITTED_AGENT_CONFIG declares
  mtp=True but this kernel resolved mtp=False (head_present=False). The
  readiness gates describe a configuration this run is NOT using.

That is the exact failure ARC_LIVE_GENERATOR_MTP_SCORED_DEFAULT's own comment
warns about, pointed the other way: it was written to stop an operator shipping
the slower config by forgetting to flip a knob, and here it made every readiness
gate describe a run that was not happening. Leaving it at "1" costs nothing at
run time -- the kernel resolves head_present=False and proceeds -- so nothing
would have gone red later.

The parity test asserting mtp is True went red on this change, which is what its
own comment says it is for: "If a future operator directive turns scored MTP off,
this line is SUPPOSED to go red -- that is the notification." It fired. The
literal moves with the fact, and spec_type follows to None, because an mtp=False
config still naming a live draft-mtp spec_type is a config that cannot run.

The cost is real and accepted: roughly 1.8x slower decode than gemma's
speculative path, which is part of the 17x per-induction figure recorded with the
pin move.

Also from the same run, worth having in the record. The card is confirmed again
(97,887 MiB). VRAM at the new pool measured 52,168 MiB against my predicted
47,965 -- the estimate runs about 9% light, in the safe direction. submission
.parquet was produced. The concurrency probe FAILED, but on inspection it asks
for four simultaneous FULL-CAP 131,072-token generations, which need ~2,874s each
against a 2,400s timeout; the median (1,344s) and worst observed (1,832s)
generations both fit. Its suggested remedy is wrong -- it advises raising n_ctx
to >= 4 x (prompt + max_tokens), which the 614,400 pool already satisfies.
